                <li class="ms-story ms-story--insight">
                  <span class="ms-story-tag">Home &middot; insight</span>
                  <p class="ms-story-text">Southampton goalkeeper Aaron Ramsdale is likely to remain at the club until the January transfer window after failing to secure a move during the summer. Despite expectations he would leave following the club&#x27;s relegation to the Championship, Ramsdale has not found a new club, with the Turkish and Saudi transfer windows closing soon. Head coach Tonda Eckert confirmed Ramsdale remains part of the squad and has had honest conversations with him about his role, emphasizing Daniel Peretz as the number one goalkeeper and George Long as second choice. Eckert acknowledged Ramsdale&#x27;s professionalism and left open the possibility of his involvement if injuries occur.</p>
                  <span class="ms-story-meta">Aaron Ramsdale&#x27;s transfer situation and squad role</span>
                  
                </li>
                
                <li class="ms-story ms-story--insight">
                  <span class="ms-story-tag">Home &middot; insight</span>
                  <p class="ms-story-text">Southampton defender James Bree renewed his contract until 2029, following the signings of Daniel Peretz and Cyle Larin. Bree expressed enthusiasm about staying at the club despite the challenges following the Spygate scandal. Head coach Tonda Eckert trusts Bree to play every game he is fit for, and Bree appreciates the confidence from the coach and fans, which boosts his and the team&#x27;s performances. Bree was voted Southern Daily Echo Player of the Year in May.</p>
                  <span class="ms-story-meta">James Bree contract renewal and squad role</span>
                  
                </li>
                
                <li class="ms-story ms-story--insight">
                  <span class="ms-story-tag">Home &middot; insight</span>
                  <p class="ms-story-text">Former Championship striker Sam Parkin praised Southampton defender Keven Schlotterbeck for his ball skills and passing range after his recent arrival from FC Augsburg. Schlotterbeck has started both games since joining and scored a goal against Birmingham City. Parkin noted Schlotterbeck&#x27;s aggressive passing and ability to play through lines, despite some defensive errors early on. Schlotterbeck&#x27;s brother Nico is an established player at Borussia Dortmund. Parkin expects Schlotterbeck to be a frequent talking point this season.</p>
                  <span class="ms-story-meta">Keven Schlotterbeck&#x27;s potential impact</span>
                  
                </li>
                
