                    <li><span class="ms-xi-num">6</span><span class="ms-xi-player">Marko Stamenić</span></li>
                    
                    <li><span class="ms-xi-num">30</span><span class="ms-xi-player">Joseph Opoku</span></li>
                    
                    <li><span class="ms-xi-num">8</span><span class="ms-xi-player">Elijah Just</span></li>
                    
                    <li><span class="ms-xi-num">49</span><span class="ms-xi-player">Moussa Kounfolo Yeo</span></li>
                    
                    <li><span class="ms-xi-num">9</span><span class="ms-xi-player">Žan Vipotnik</span></li>
                    
                  </ul>
                  
                </div>
                
              </div>
            </section>

            <section class="ms-pane ms-pane--pred">
              <div class="ms-pane-head">
                <span class="ms-pane-title">Prediction</span>
                <span class="ms-pane-note">1X2</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ms-pred-pick">
                <div>
                  <span class="ms-pred-label">Model pick</span>
                  <div class="ms-pred-choice">Draw or Southampton win</div>
                </div>
                
              </div>
              <p class="ms-pred-why">Southampton have a strong home record and recent good form at St. Mary&#x27;s, including a big 5-1 win over Millwall, while Swansea are top of the Championship and unbeaten away but have some key injuries. The head-to-head favors Southampton historically, especially at home. Market odds slightly favor Southampton but with a close draw possibility. Considering squad strength, home advantage, and recent performances, Southampton are likely to avoid defeat, but Swansea&#x27;s quality suggests a draw is also plausible.</p>
            </section>

          </div>
        </article>
        
