  <script id="msStorylineData" type="application/json">{"2026090826111": [{"kind": "insight", "text": "The match is a Champions League playoff with high stakes, featuring Lille hosting Betis, who recently defeated Real Madrid, adding pressure and intensity to the encounter.", "meta": "Preview insight about the Champions League playoff match", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille benefits from five days of rest after their recent Ligue 1 win against Toulouse before hosting Betis.", "meta": "Rest considerations for Lille ahead of the upcoming match", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Betis recently defeated Real Madrid 1-0, highlighting their strong form heading into this match.", "meta": "Form considerations for Betis after Real Madrid win (a prior group game)", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille's main tactical uncertainty is the number 9 position, with Olivier Giroud and Ayase Ueda both expected to play but the order of their deployment is unclear.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Lille's number 9 position for the upcoming match", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Ethan Mbapp\u00e9 is expected to keep his place on the right side of Lille's attack.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Ethan Mbapp\u00e9's role for the upcoming match", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille will play eight Champions League group stage matches, four at home and four away. Their home matches include a fixture against Real Bayern Munich on November 25 and the opening group match against Real Betis on September 8. The group stage campaign starts in September and ends in January with an away match at AS Roma.", "meta": "Lille's Champions League group stage schedule", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille's electronic ticketing system failed minutes before their home match against PSG, leaving hundreds of fans unable to access their seats and causing a 15-minute delay to kickoff. The club apologized for the disruption and faced criticism on social media for the incident. The Ligue de Football Professionnel approved the delayed start to allow affected supporters to enter the stadium.", "meta": "Ticketing system failure at Stade Pierre-Mauroy", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "After Lille conceded a late equalizer against PSG, club president Olivier L\u00e9tang called the refereeing a 'scandal' due to excessive added time. Players Nabil Bentaleb and Romain Perraud also expressed frustration about the extended stoppage time that allowed PSG to score twice in the final minutes. Lille had led 2-0 before PSG's late comeback.", "meta": "Lille's reaction to refereeing controversy after Lille-PSG match", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Carlo Ancelotti, current Brazil national team coach, attended Lille's home match against PSG to support his son Davide Ancelotti, Lille's head coach. Davide recently joined Lille after working as his father's assistant with Brazil and previously served as PSG's fitness coach when Carlo was manager there.", "meta": "Carlo Ancelotti supporting son Davide at Lille", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille's Stade Pierre-Mauroy was nearly sold out for the home match against PSG, with an expected attendance between 48,000 and 49,000. The club set a new record with 33,500 season ticket holders for the 2026-2027 season, a 60% increase over five years, ranking third in France behind Marseille and PSG. This surge in popularity is partly due to Lille's participation in the Champions League group stage.", "meta": "Lille's fan attendance and season ticket records", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Ahead of their home match against PSG, Lille lost key midfielder Ayyoub Bouaddi to Manchester City in a record transfer. Matias Fernandez-Pardo is sidelined from the squad until the end of the transfer window due to his desire to leave. Benjamin Andr\u00e9 and Matias Fernandez-Pardo returned to training, while Hamza Igamane remains injured. New signing Tanguy Nianzou could be available for selection.", "meta": "Lille squad news and transfer updates before PSG match", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille coach Davide Ancelotti confirmed that Matias Fernandez-Pardo will not train or play with the first team until his transfer situation is resolved by the September 1 deadline. Fernandez-Pardo, under contract until 2029, wants to leave Lille and has been linked with Atl\u00e9tico Madrid, Newcastle, and Leipzig. The club insists no player has been given a guaranteed exit.", "meta": "Matias Fernandez-Pardo sidelined until transfer resolution", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille was drawn in a challenging Champions League group with Bayern Munich, Real Betis, Galatasaray, and Slovan Bratislava at home, and away matches against Arsenal, AS Roma, Bodo/Glimt, and Stuttgart. The group stage begins in September with Lille hosting Betis on September 8.", "meta": "Lille's Champions League group opponents", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Lille announced a new five-year agreement with the Alsace-based Kronenbourg brewery to supply beers at the Stade Pierre Mauroy. The deal includes the promotion of Anostek\u00e9, a local beer brand from the Hauts-de-France region. The partnership covers all stadium hospitality areas and 40 public sales points. The announcement sparked some fan criticism on social media due to the brewery's location outside the Nord region.", "meta": "Lille's new stadium beverage partnership", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Davide Ancelotti should have a fresh, rested group available for Lille's Champions League league phase meeting with Betis Seville on Tuesday at 21:00.", "meta": "Davide Ancelotti, manager of Lille", "scope": "Home", "context": "Ancelotti on squad freshness for the upcoming match"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Without kidding, it's a scandal!", "meta": "Olivier L\u00e9tang, Lille president", "scope": "Home", "context": "Post-match comments in the stadium corridors after Lille-PSG 2-2 draw"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We were at the end of a match with a lot of intensity and concentration. For me, I think the match should have ended a bit earlier. But the referee decided to add time so we had to stay focused until the end.", "meta": "Nabil Bentaleb, Lille midfielder", "scope": "Home", "context": "Post-match interview after Lille-PSG 2-2 draw"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "There is a lot of disappointment and frustration. We felt we had the match in hand but they came back. It's hard to swallow tonight honestly. The refereeing? Apparently, there was one minute and fifteen seconds too much... I don't know, it's not for me to talk about that, but we definitely have a bitter taste.", "meta": "Romain Perraud, Lille defender", "scope": "Home", "context": "Post-match interview after Lille-PSG 2-2 draw"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We have taken the decision with the club that he will not train with the group until the end of the transfer window, until his situation is resolved. This is a transfer issue and I am focused on the players available for tomorrow who train with the group.", "meta": "Davide Ancelotti, Lille head coach", "scope": "Home", "context": "Pre-match press conference before Lille-PSG match"}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Betis fans from Pe\u00f1a B\u00e9tica Tajo 13 used boats on the Guadalquivir river to reach La Cartuja stadium for the match against Real Madrid, avoiding usual traffic jams. This alternative travel method was previously used during the Copa del Rey final and offers fans a unique and efficient way to arrive together without road congestion.", "meta": "Betis fans' alternative travel to La Cartuja", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "After defeating Real Madrid 1-0, Betis' official social media accounts posted several mocking messages targeting Real Madrid and Jos\u00e9 Mourinho, highlighting their victory and breaking Madrid's winning streak under Mourinho. The posts included playful jabs at Madrid players and referenced Betis as the 'real' team.", "meta": "Betis social media reactions after win over Real Madrid", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Manuel Pellegrini set Betis with four midfielders, two attacking fullbacks, and a mobile striker Troy Parrott to disrupt Real Madrid's defense. Betis pressed man-to-man and focused on possession control. The strategy helped Betis contain Madrid's attack and secure a 1-0 victory.", "meta": "Betis tactical setup and match approach vs Real Madrid", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "\u00c1lvaro Valles was the hero for Betis by making crucial saves including a penalty stop against Kylian Mbapp\u00e9 in added time. Troy Parrott scored the only goal after capitalizing on a rebound from Courtois. Betis held off a strong Real Madrid attack to claim a 1-0 victory.", "meta": "\u00c1lvaro Valles and Troy Parrott key roles in Betis win", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Manuel Pellegrini deployed an offensive lineup including Isco, Antony, Fornals, and 'Cucho' Hern\u00e1ndez. \u00c1lvaro Fidalgo made his season debut as a substitute. Troy Parrott scored the winning goal after a rebound from Courtois. Betis defended well and \u00c1lvaro Valles made crucial saves including a penalty stop to secure a 1-0 victory.", "meta": "Betis tactical performance and player contributions vs Real Madrid", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I only know one Real. Real Betis Balompi\u00e9.", "meta": "Real Betis official social media", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match social media message after win over Real Madrid"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Well, another year more.", "meta": "Real Betis official social media", "scope": "Away", "context": "Response to DjMaRiiO's comment about Madrid not winning at Betis since Gareth Bale played"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "90 minutes at La Cartuja are very long.", "meta": "Real Betis official social media", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match message adapting a famous Real Madrid slogan"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "You shall not pass.", "meta": "Real Betis official social media", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match message highlighting H\u00e9ctor Beller\u00edn's defensive performance against Vinicius Junior"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Confrontation with the best of Turkey... Defeated.", "meta": "Real Betis official social media", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match message about Arda G\u00fcler's defeat"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Allow me to introduce the first team to defeat Jos\u00e9 Mourinho's Real Madrid.", "meta": "Real Betis official social media", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match message celebrating Betis as the first team to beat Mourinho's Madrid in this spell"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Playing against Real Madrid, VAR and a sending-off, all together, is difficult. The whole world knows how VAR are handled.", "meta": "Manuel Pellegrini, manager of Betis", "scope": "Away", "context": "Betis manager on challenges against Real Madrid (a prior group game)"}], "2026090812079": [{"kind": "insight", "text": "Matches against Instituto are tense encounters that occupy the players' and staff's minds throughout the weekend.", "meta": "Preview insight about tense encounters between Union de Santa Fe and Instituto", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Leonardo Madelon must make at least two forced changes and is considering a third unexpected modification for Union de Santa Fe's lineup against Instituto.", "meta": "Lineup considerations for Madelon ahead of the upcoming match", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Union de Santa Fe reached an agreement with their employees and the UTEDyC union to resolve salary payment delays and reinstate staff previously excluded due to budget cuts. This resolution occurred just before the match against Instituto. Squad-wise, Tom\u00e1s Fagioli is expected to replace Maizon Rodr\u00edguez in defense, and Ignacio Malcorra will start in midfield for the injured Mauro Luna Diale. Joaqu\u00edn Mosqueira has recovered and may be considered as an alternative due to Lucas Menossi's physical condition.", "meta": "Union de Santa Fe's off-pitch employee resolution and squad update", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Union de Santa Fe will face Instituto at the 15 de Abril stadium aiming to continue their recent recovery after two consecutive wins. The team seeks to prove they can compete equally against one of the best-performing teams. Union currently holds seventh place in Zone A and aims to maintain their playoff position by securing another victory. The match also has implications for qualification to international cups, with Instituto being a direct competitor in the accumulated table.", "meta": "Union de Santa Fe ahead of the upcoming match", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Nicol\u00e1s Lamolina has been appointed as the referee for Union de Santa Fe's match against Instituto. He has a long history officiating Union's matches, including recent wins against Lan\u00fas and Independiente Rivadavia. Lamolina has overseen 22 matches involving Union with a record of eight wins, nine draws, and five losses for the team. Juan Pablo Loustau will serve as VAR. The match is a key fixture for Union as they seek to continue their positive run.", "meta": "Referee Nicol\u00e1s Lamolina's appointment for Union de Santa Fe vs Instituto", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Union de Santa Fe is close to finalizing the sale of Maizon Rodr\u00edguez to Krasnodar in Russia for around 4 million dollars, with Union owning 50% of the player's rights. The club expects to receive about 2 million dollars net. The transfer deadline for replacements is September 9. Meanwhile, Lautaro Vargas is undergoing surgery and will be out for the season. The club is evaluating options to reinforce the squad, especially in defensive positions. Mauro Luna Diale's injury is also under assessment, with Ignacio Malcorra stepping up in recent matches.", "meta": "Maizon Rodr\u00edguez's transfer and squad implications for Union de Santa Fe", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Ignacio Malcorra scored for Union de Santa Fe at the 15 de Abril stadium for the first time in over ten years, marking a significant moment in his career. He entered the match against Sarmiento due to an injury to Mauro Luna Diale and contributed decisively with a goal and an assist, helping secure a 4-1 victory. Malcorra's previous goal at the stadium was in February 2016, and his recent performance highlights his importance to the team.", "meta": "Ignacio Malcorra's goal return at 15 de Abril", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Union de Santa Fe defeated Sarmiento 4-1 at the 15 de Abril stadium. Cristian Tarragona scored twice, Ignacio Malcorra scored a spectacular free-kick goal and provided an assist, and Eric Ram\u00edrez added the fourth goal. The team showed a combination of collective solidity and individual quality. Sarmiento managed a late consolation goal but Union controlled the match throughout. The victory marked Union's second consecutive win and boosted their confidence.", "meta": "Recap of Union de Santa Fe's 4-1 win over Sarmiento (a prior league game)", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Cristian Tarragona is the top Argentine scorer in 2026 with 15 goals across all competitions, including 5 in the current Torneo Clausura. He scored twice in consecutive matches against Aldosivi and Sarmiento, helping Union de Santa Fe secure important victories. Tarragona's recent scoring surge has been crucial for the team's improved offensive output and confidence. His performance has made him a key player and fan favorite at the club.", "meta": "Cristian Tarragona's goal-scoring form at Union de Santa Fe", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We lacked goal-scoring chances,\" Tarragona said after a previous match, \"but the response came in the best way I know: with goals.", "meta": "Cristian Tarragona, striker", "scope": "Home", "context": "Post-match interview after scoring goals for Union de Santa Fe"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "These matches are tense, they have you thinking about them all weekend.", "meta": "Leonardo Madelon, manager of Union de Santa Fe", "scope": "Home", "context": "Madelon on match tension ahead of the upcoming match"}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba arrives at the match against Uni\u00f3n de Santa Fe in a positive moment after a 1-0 victory over San Lorenzo. They are one of the top contenders in the Torneo Clausura Zone A with 16 points. A win away would reinforce their status as a title candidate. The match is scheduled for September 7, 2026, at the Estadio 15 de Abril and will be broadcast on TNT Sports Premium.", "meta": "Instituto ahead of the upcoming match against Uni\u00f3n de Santa Fe", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Alex Luna, a key player and one of Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba's most influential figures, was subject to transfer rumors during the recent market. Despite interest from clubs in Brazil and Mexico, Instituto's president Juan Manuel Cavagliatto rejected offers, prioritizing sporting objectives over immediate sales. Luna is expected to remain with Instituto for the foreseeable future, maintaining squad strength for upcoming fixtures.", "meta": "Instituto's player Alex Luna transfer situation ahead of the upcoming match", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Mat\u00edas Gallardo, a 22-year-old attacking midfielder for Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba, is recognized for his creativity, tactical intelligence, and versatility. Son of Marcelo Gallardo, he has become a key player in Instituto's strong campaign in the Torneo Clausura. Mat\u00edas has played 18 matches this season, scoring one goal and providing one assist. He is known for his work ethic and ability to contribute both offensively and defensively.", "meta": "Profile of Mat\u00edas Gallardo, Instituto player", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "After Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba defeated San Lorenzo 1-0, San Lorenzo's management and coach N\u00e9stor Gorosito mutually agreed to terminate his contract. Gorosito's tenure lasted only 60 days with a record of two wins, one draw, and four losses. The defeat to Instituto was a significant factor in this decision.", "meta": "Impact of Instituto's win on San Lorenzo's coaching situation", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "San Lorenzo announced the departure of coach N\u00e9stor Gorosito following a 1-0 defeat to Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba. The club's management cited poor results including elimination from Copa Argentina and a loss in the local derby. Walter Perazzo was named to lead upcoming training sessions.", "meta": "San Lorenzo coach dismissal following loss to Instituto", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba prepared to face San Lorenzo with a starting lineup including Marcos Ledesma, Leonel Mosevich, Fernando Alarc\u00f3n, Jonathan Galv\u00e1n, Mat\u00edas Gallardo, Gustavo Abreg\u00fa, Diego Sosa, Giuliano Cerato, Mat\u00edas Tissera, Alex Luna, and Jhon C\u00f3rdoba under coach Diego Flores. The match was set at Estadio Juan Domingo Per\u00f3n with the aim to maintain their strong position in the Torneo Clausura.", "meta": "Instituto's lineup and tactical setup ahead of a prior league game", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Instituto de C\u00f3rdoba maintained the top position in Zone A of the Torneo Clausura 2026 after a 0-0 draw with Atl\u00e9tico Tucum\u00e1n. They led the group with 13 points, one ahead of V\u00e9lez and Gimnasia de Mendoza. The tournament format includes 30 clubs divided into two groups, with playoffs for the top eight teams in each group.", "meta": "Instituto's position as group leader in Torneo Clausura 2026", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Instituto plays aggressively to quickly recover possession and maintains a very firm defensive structure.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Instituto's aggressive ball recovery and defense", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Instituto had difficulty breaking down Union de Santa Fe's defensive plan in the first half.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Instituto struggling against Union de Santa Fe defense", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I identify with my father's style because I am a player with good passing, who thinks and... I am fast.", "meta": "Mat\u00edas Gallardo, Instituto midfielder", "scope": "Away", "context": "Interview discussing his playing style and influences"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Losing is very ugly. When you can't get out, it gets difficult,", "meta": "N\u00e9stor Gorosito, former San Lorenzo coach", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match press conference after loss to Instituto"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "That (resigning) does not cross my mind.", "meta": "N\u00e9stor Gorosito, former San Lorenzo coach", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match press conference after loss to Instituto"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "San Lorenzo informs that N\u00e9stor Gorosito will no longer continue as the first division team's coach. By mutual agreement, the contractual relationship with the club has been terminated.", "meta": "San Lorenzo club statement", "scope": "Away", "context": "Official club announcement on social media"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "In the first half we were uncomfortable in unlocking their defensive plan.", "meta": "Diego Flores, manager of Instituto", "scope": "Away", "context": "Instituto manager on first-half defensive challenges in recent Primera Division game"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "The team plays aggressively to quickly recover the ball and is very firm defensively.", "meta": "Diego Flores, manager of Instituto", "scope": "Away", "context": "Instituto manager on aggressive and firm defensive style"}], "2026090913506": [{"kind": "insight", "text": "The quarterfinal first leg between Boca Juniors and S\u00e3o Paulo is a highly important South American football classic, with both teams aware of the historical rivalry and the difficulty of the two-legged tie.", "meta": "Preview insight about the upcoming quarterfinal match between Boca Juniors and S\u00e3o Paulo", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Boca Juniors reached the quarterfinals after eliminating O\u2019Higgins and Recoleta, and the first leg will be played at La Bombonera, with the return leg at Morumbi a week later.", "meta": "Boca Juniors' Copa Sudamericana quarterfinal path and venue details", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo comes into the match after a convincing 2-0 win over Atl\u00e9tico-MG, their first clean sheet since the World Cup break, which boosted confidence and defensive solidity.", "meta": "S\u00e3o Paulo's confidence boost from recent Serie A clean sheet win", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo's coach emphasized the need to reach their maximum effort to secure qualification, highlighting the high stakes and competitive nature of the Copa Sudamericana quarterfinal.", "meta": "Preview insight about S\u00e3o Paulo's qualification focus for the upcoming match", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Boca Juniors' lineup for the match includes some uncertainty in central defense and attack, with options between Facundo Herrera or Marco Pellegrino in defense and Leonel Flores or Sebasti\u00e1n Villa in attack, indicating tactical flexibility or adaptation by Arruabarrena.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Boca Juniors' defensive and attacking lineup options", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Leandro Paredes was on the bench due to the need caused by other players with fevers. He is recovering well and trained normally yesterday; otherwise, I would not have taken him to the bench. However, we must take logical care with a player coming from prolonged inactivity. When there is such an intense sequence of matches, it is normal to feel tired.", "meta": "Rodolfo Arruabarrena, manager of Boca Juniors", "scope": "Home", "context": "Pellegrino on Leandro Paredes' fitness ahead of the upcoming match"}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo has been using a three-center-back system, which was effective in their recent 2-0 win over Atl\u00e9tico-MG, maintaining a high defensive line and pressing high to disrupt the opponent's build-up.", "meta": "Tactical insight on S\u00e3o Paulo's three-center-back system in Serie A", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Dorival J\u00fanior has shown tactical flexibility by rotating players and maintaining the three-center-back formation, with attacking players like Gustavo Santana and Luciano alternating roles to create movement and unpredictability.", "meta": "Tactical insight on S\u00e3o Paulo's attacking rotation and flexibility", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo defeated Atl\u00e9tico-MG 2-0 at Morumbi with goals from Luciano and Iago Borduchi. Luciano reached 116 goals for the club, surpassing Careca. The team secured its second consecutive league win, distancing itself from relegation threats. Atl\u00e9tico-MG rested key players due to other competitions. S\u00e3o Paulo prepares to face Boca Juniors in Buenos Aires in the Copa Sudamericana quarterfinals on September 8.", "meta": "Recap of S\u00e3o Paulo's win over Atl\u00e9tico-MG and upcoming Boca Juniors match", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo ended Atl\u00e9tico-MG's 14-match unbeaten streak by winning 2-0 at Morumbi. The team controlled the first half and scored in the second with Luciano and Iago Borduchi. Atl\u00e9tico-MG increased pressure in the second half but failed to score. S\u00e3o Paulo's defense kept a clean sheet for the first time in ten matches. Both teams will next play in the Copa Sudamericana quarterfinals.", "meta": "Detailed recap of S\u00e3o Paulo's 2-0 win over Atl\u00e9tico-MG", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Coach Dorival J\u00fanior announced S\u00e3o Paulo's starting eleven for the match against Atl\u00e9tico-MG, including Rafael in goal and a defensive line of Domingos Duarte, Arboleda, and Sabino. Midfielders Lucas Ramon, Danielzinho, Marcos Ant\u00f4nio, and Wendell were selected, with an attack featuring Luciano, Arthur, and Gustavo Santana. Calleri was on the bench recovering from an ankle sprain. Volante Newton was available after injury recovery. The match was important for S\u00e3o Paulo to consolidate its position in the league.", "meta": "S\u00e3o Paulo lineup and injury news before Atl\u00e9tico-MG match", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Carlos Sadi, a S\u00e3o Paulo councilor and vice-presidential candidate, made elitist and prejudiced remarks about the club's fanbase and neighborhoods associated with it. His comments sparked outrage among fans and led to his withdrawal from the vice-presidential race. The statements highlighted tensions within the club's administration and its relationship with its diverse supporters.", "meta": "Controversy over S\u00e3o Paulo councilor's statements", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Roberto, an 82-year-old S\u00e3o Paulo fan, overcame a heart attack, prostate cancer, three strokes, and severe mobility limitations to attend a match at Morumbi. He has supported S\u00e3o Paulo for decades, attending the stadium's partial inauguration in 1960. He cherishes the club's Libertadores titles and praises former coach Tel\u00ea Santana. Despite current administrative difficulties, his passion for S\u00e3o Paulo remains strong.", "meta": "Longtime S\u00e3o Paulo fan's story at Morumbi", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo's president of the Deliberative Council, Olten Ayres, created a commission to analyze a contract with Ticketmaster for managing Morumbi stadium tickets. The contract, crucial for advancing R$140 million to pay player debts, faced challenges from competitor NewC, which questioned the bidding process. S\u00e3o Paulo maintains Ticketmaster's offer was the best official proposal. The contract awaits approval from club governance bodies.", "meta": "S\u00e3o Paulo's ticketing contract dispute", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo faces a severe financial crisis with debts nearing R$1 billion. President Harry Massis urged the Deliberative Council to urgently vote on a proposal to clear salary arrears, which range from two to four months. The club plans to use funds from a Ticketmaster contract to regularize payments by the end of September. Without council approval, funds remain blocked, risking further instability during the season.", "meta": "S\u00e3o Paulo's financial crisis and salary issues", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We are already naturally studying the opposing team and trying to field the best possible team for Tuesday's game. It is a fundamental, very important match, a great South American football classic. I think we all know a bit of the history of both teams and I have no doubt that we will have two very complicated matches. I hope we can play a great game and achieve qualification, which will be fundamental for our continuity.", "meta": "Junior Dorival, manager of Sao Paulo", "scope": "Away", "context": "Dorival J\u00fanior on squad selection for the upcoming match"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We will have to reach our limit, our maximum, in pursuit of our qualification. A team that deserves our respect and consideration because it has very high-level players, very well coached, and is also seeking a path, just like S\u00e3o Paulo. I hope we can play a great game.", "meta": "Junior Dorival, manager of Sao Paulo", "scope": "Away", "context": "Dorival J\u00fanior on the challenge of Boca Juniors ahead of the upcoming match"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We are not going to preserve players against Boca Juniors. If necessary, we will change what I am thinking for the match there. We are already naturally studying the opposing team and trying to field the best possible team for Tuesday's game, a fundamental, very important match, a great South American football classic.", "meta": "Junior Dorival, manager of Sao Paulo", "scope": "Away", "context": "Dorival J\u00fanior on no player preservation against Boca Juniors"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "S\u00e3o Paulo lost its glamour. If I didn't have glamour, I would root for Corinthians and go to Itaquera, not pray at Morumbi. Sorry, I am really elitist.", "meta": "Carlos Sadi, S\u00e3o Paulo councilor", "scope": "Away", "context": "Interview with S\u00e3o Paulo Digital"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I was used to S\u00e3o Paulo of Paulo Planet Buarque, Brasil Vita, and now you put the lower class to work here. Sorry, you married a woman from Parais\u00f3polis and the whole family is living with you.", "meta": "Carlos Sadi, S\u00e3o Paulo councilor", "scope": "Away", "context": "Interview with S\u00e3o Paulo Digital"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I thought I wouldn't have time anymore. But I did.", "meta": "Roberto, longtime S\u00e3o Paulo fan", "scope": "Away", "context": "Interview about returning to Morumbi despite health challenges"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "All were intense, but the ones that marked me the most were the two Libertadores. The team was really good, had an excellent coach, Tel\u00ea Santana, and great players.", "meta": "Roberto, longtime S\u00e3o Paulo fan", "scope": "Away", "context": "Reflecting on memorable club achievements"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I regret very much that S\u00e3o Paulo is going through this administrative situation. I feel for S\u00e3o Paulo, which is a powerhouse and has set better examples before.", "meta": "Roberto, longtime S\u00e3o Paulo fan", "scope": "Away", "context": "Commenting on current club administration"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I need you to help pressure the Council president to put this issue to a vote. Without a vote, we won't meet our obligations. This must be done urgently.", "meta": "Harry Massis, S\u00e3o Paulo president", "scope": "Away", "context": "Leaked audio urging council action on salary payments"}], "2026090818750": [{"kind": "insight", "text": "Southampton goalkeeper Aaron Ramsdale is likely to remain at the club until the January transfer window after failing to secure a move during the summer. Despite expectations he would leave following the club's relegation to the Championship, Ramsdale has not found a new club, with the Turkish and Saudi transfer windows closing soon. Head coach Tonda Eckert confirmed Ramsdale remains part of the squad and has had honest conversations with him about his role, emphasizing Daniel Peretz as the number one goalkeeper and George Long as second choice. Eckert acknowledged Ramsdale's professionalism and left open the possibility of his involvement if injuries occur.", "meta": "Aaron Ramsdale's transfer situation and squad role", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Southampton defender James Bree renewed his contract until 2029, following the signings of Daniel Peretz and Cyle Larin. Bree expressed enthusiasm about staying at the club despite the challenges following the Spygate scandal. Head coach Tonda Eckert trusts Bree to play every game he is fit for, and Bree appreciates the confidence from the coach and fans, which boosts his and the team's performances. Bree was voted Southern Daily Echo Player of the Year in May.", "meta": "James Bree contract renewal and squad role", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Former Championship striker Sam Parkin praised Southampton defender Keven Schlotterbeck for his ball skills and passing range after his recent arrival from FC Augsburg. Schlotterbeck has started both games since joining and scored a goal against Birmingham City. Parkin noted Schlotterbeck's aggressive passing and ability to play through lines, despite some defensive errors early on. Schlotterbeck's brother Nico is an established player at Borussia Dortmund. Parkin expects Schlotterbeck to be a frequent talking point this season.", "meta": "Keven Schlotterbeck's potential impact", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Southampton Football Club announced a new multi-year partnership with global online trading brand VARIANSE, granting the company worldwide rights to use the club's intellectual property in international branding. The partnership includes matchday advertising at St Mary's Stadium and digital campaigns featuring the men's first team. VARIANSE aims to expand its international presence and collaborate with Southampton on engaging content for the club's global fanbase and the Hampshire community. Club chief revenue officer Greg Baker highlighted the alignment of values between the club and VARIANSE.", "meta": "Southampton's VARIANSE sponsorship deal", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "In the summer of 2006, Southampton manager George Burley rebuilt the squad with international players, veterans, and future club icons following relegation. Key signings included goalkeeper Kelvin Davis, who became a club great with over 300 appearances, and Bradley Wright-Phillips, who scored important goals. Other arrivals were Jhon Vi\u00e1fara, Rudi Sk\u00e1cel, I\u00f1igo Idi\u00e1kez, Mario Li\u010dka, and Pel\u00e9. The new squad played attacking football and finished sixth, reaching the play-offs but losing to Derby County on penalties. This transfer window marked a turning point for Southampton's modern era.", "meta": "George Burley's 2006 Southampton signings", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Southampton defender Keven Schlotterbeck made a solid debut after joining from FC Augsburg for \u00a33 million. Head coach Tonda Eckert started Schlotterbeck ahead of captain Jack Stephens, assigning him the task of marking Millwall's striker Josh Coburn man-to-man. Schlotterbeck made 11 defensive contributions, showing aggression and reliability. His left foot helps Southampton open play on both sides from the back. He communicated well with teammates and fit into the Championship style effectively.", "meta": "Keven Schlotterbeck's debut and performance", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Midfielder James Ward-Prowse expressed joy about returning to Southampton, highlighting his family's excitement and connection to the club. His children wore Saints kits and enjoyed being part of the club environment. Ward-Prowse, who left Southampton for West Ham in 2023, has remained based in Hampshire with his family. He acknowledged the strong bond with the club and hopes his son can follow in his footsteps. Ward-Prowse aims to help Southampton return to the Premier League after re-signing on a two-year deal.", "meta": "James Ward-Prowse's return and family connection", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "James Ward-Prowse stated he is physically and mentally prepared to make an immediate impact at Southampton after signing a two-year deal. He expressed eagerness to play and contribute to the club's promotion push. Ward-Prowse reflected on his previous departure and challenges at West Ham, Nottingham Forest, and Burnley, emphasizing his determination to fight back and show his quality. He acknowledged changes in management affected his playing time but remains proud of overcoming difficulties and returning to Southampton.", "meta": "James Ward-Prowse's readiness and motivation", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Southampton reached an agreement with West Ham United to re-sign midfielder James Ward-Prowse for a fee under \u00a31 million. Ward-Prowse, who spent his entire senior career at Southampton before moving to West Ham in 2023, is set to return to boost Southampton's Championship promotion campaign. The 31-year-old has made 410 appearances for Southampton, scoring 55 goals and providing 52 assists. The deal could be completed in time for Ward-Prowse to make his second debut against Millwall. Southampton currently face a points deduction following the Spygate scandal.", "meta": "James Ward-Prowse re-signing deal", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Southampton Football Club celebrated 25 years at St Mary's Stadium, which hosted its first competitive game on 25 August 2001. Fans and club historian Duncan Holley recalled the move from The Dell, noting the emotional mix of sadness and excitement. The stadium's atmosphere grew over time, with memorable moments including Sadio Man\u00e9's fastest Premier League hat-trick in 2015 and a key play-off semi-final win in 2024. Fans remain a steady element, maintaining traditions and songs despite the move to a modern venue.", "meta": "Southampton's St Mary's Stadium 25-year reflections", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "He [Peretz] is number one, and that stands. He deserves that. He's had some brilliant performances in the last year and now towards the beginning of the season. My commitment to Long has a number two stance as well and I think that group has worked very, very well last year together with Jamie [Jones]. With Rambo, we've had honest conversations from the first day of pre-season until the very last day of the transfer window. He's a part of the group, just like everyone else. Everyone is playing his role, the expectations for him are clear: to support the team in the best way. He's been very professional in doing that. That's all there is to say.", "meta": "Tonda Eckert, Southampton head coach", "scope": "Home", "context": "Pre-match press conference ahead of league clash against Lincoln City"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I always felt that if the contract was there and we could talk about it, it was always something I was looking to do, and that didn't change in my mind. Daniel and Cyle signed a couple of days before all my stuff got sorted, so I saw them come through when I was still in the process of sorting things. But I think that gave me a little bit of a buzz as well to know that the boys were all coming back together, and I think it's nice to keep the group together.", "meta": "James Bree, Southampton defender", "scope": "Home", "context": "Interview about contract renewal and squad atmosphere"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "James played almost every single game last year. I have big trust in James.", "meta": "Tonda Eckert, Southampton head coach", "scope": "Home", "context": "Comment on Bree's role in the team"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Schlotterbeck is a name we're going to be talking about quite a lot. He's the older brother of the lad who's at Dortmund. He's got a lovely left foot, Schlotterbeck, and he was arguably Southampton's best player, scored the goal. However, he made two howling errors despite all that. One, [Jay] Stansfield nicked the ball off him on the halfway line, went 1v1, hit the base of the post, and then in the second half, he missed the opportunity, a carbon copy, trying to play out and got dispossessed. But he's got really nice range of passing, kind of through the lines, punches it into the midfield players and the frontmen, really aggressive despite not being towering.", "meta": "Sam Parkin, former Championship striker", "scope": "Home", "context": "Commentary on Schlotterbeck's early performances for Southampton"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "We are delighted to welcome VARIANSE to Southampton FC as our Official Global Trading Partner. The partnership reflects Southampton FC's long-standing commitment to working with ambitious, high-growth brands that share the club's values of authenticity, innovation, community engagement and a strong focus on their clients and supporters.", "meta": "Greg Baker, Southampton chief revenue officer", "scope": "Home", "context": "Statement on new sponsorship partnership"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Becoming Southampton FC's Official Global Trading Partner is a pivotal moment for VARIANSE. Southampton has a proud history, an international fan base and a strong reputation for developing talent and embracing innovation. Those qualities reflect the ethos that has shaped the way we have built VARIANSE. Trading at a high level demands preparation, technology, discipline and the ability to perform when it matters. We see many of those same principles in elite sport, which makes Southampton a natural partner for us. We're looking forward to working closely with the club and creating engaging content and experiences that bring the partnership to life for supporters around the world.", "meta": "Rohit Mirpuri, CEO of VARIANSE", "scope": "Home", "context": "Statement on partnership with Southampton FC"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "The kids were all running around last night in the garden in their Saints kits. I think that's all you need to know. For them to experience it here is really special. To see my son now, joking around here yesterday, pretending to sign a contract and hold the shirt up. He's living it through me, which is really special. Hopefully, he can follow in my footsteps. It's nice to have that love around the club - they felt it as well.", "meta": "James Ward-Prowse, Southampton midfielder", "scope": "Home", "context": "Interview about family reaction to his return"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I have been controlling what I can, and that's to be prepared physically and mentally to come in and do the job required. I've been waiting to play, to be part of a club and to feel that love and that want from the fans. I'm looking forward to stepping out there again. Even when I left, there was probably that narrative building that, 'Oh, he'll return one day', and football is a funny game and works in weird ways. When things go the way they do, and opportunities arise, coming back here was not somewhere that you have to second-guess about.", "meta": "James Ward-Prowse, Southampton midfielder", "scope": "Home", "context": "Pre-match interview ahead of Millwall game"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I've been really proud of how I've dealt with those challenges. It's not been easy, but I'm here now, looking forward to representing Southampton again.", "meta": "James Ward-Prowse, Southampton midfielder", "scope": "Home", "context": "Pre-match interview ahead of Millwall game"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "It sort of proved that the fans are the steady element amongst everything. We might move house, we might move ground, but it's the actual fans that remain the same, the songs that remain the same.", "meta": "Martin Sanders, Southampton fan channel operator", "scope": "Home", "context": "Reflecting on the significance of St Mary's Stadium"}], "2026090839583": [{"kind": "insight", "text": "Volos feels they have not received the results they deserved in recent matches and must focus on upcoming games.", "meta": "Preview insight about Volos' recent results and focus", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "The match is competitive with Volos showing resilience to come back from behind, but also under pressure to improve effectiveness and avoid self-inflicted setbacks.", "meta": "Preview insight about Volos' resilience and pressure to improve effectiveness", "scope": "Match", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Olympiacos owner Vangelis Marinakis confirmed the club will cover the entire cost of the new Karaiskakis stadium construction, estimated at 250 million euros, without state funding. The project dossier has been approved by the Ministry of Environment, pending legislative changes for the metal roof height and a 49-year stadium usage extension. The Hellenic Olympic Committee supports the plan and will sign a lease contract with Olympiacos. Construction is planned to start in May 2027.", "meta": "Olympiacos Piraeus new Karaiskakis stadium project update", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Olympiacos announced that tickets for their home match against Volos Elabet on September 8, 2026, will be sold exclusively online via the club's official website starting September 4 at 18:00 until sold out or match start. Entry to the Karaiskakis Stadium will be only via the Gov.gr Wallet app using QR codes. Special instructions apply for minors and foreign fans without Greek tax codes, including on-site ticket office availability on match day.", "meta": "Olympiacos Piraeus ticketing instructions for upcoming match", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Olympiacos submitted their Europa League squad list to UEFA for the League Phase starting September 16, 2026, against Jagiellonia at Karaiskakis Stadium. Coach Jos\u00e9 Luis Mendilibar included 21 players, excluding Popovic, Garcia, Sipioni, and Roca, as well as Roman Yaremchuk and Clayton. New signings Gustavo Puerta, Leon Bailey, and Armando Gonzalez are included. The club's European schedule includes home matches against Jagiellonia, Sparta Prague, Milan, and Hoffenheim, and away matches against Marseille, Rennes, Celje, and Torense.", "meta": "Olympiacos Piraeus Europa League squad and fixtures", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Olympiacos announced that tickets for their home league match against OFI on September 12, 2026, will be sold exclusively online starting September 2 at 13:00 until sold out or match start. Entry to the Karaiskakis Stadium will be only via the Gov.gr Wallet app using QR codes. Guardians must add tickets for minors under 15 to their wallet. Foreign fans without Greek tax codes must select 'Non Greek Resident' and verify identity with passport NFC scanning. On match day, ticket offices at Gate 25 will assist fans unable to complete digital verification.", "meta": "Olympiacos Piraeus ticketing for home league match vs OFI", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Gustavo Puerta, a 23-year-old midfielder, has reached a verbal agreement to join Nottingham Forest (English club) and will be immediately loaned to Olympiacos Piraeus for the 2026-27 season. Nottingham Forest will pay his release clause to Racing Santander (Spanish club). Puerta will sign a contract with Nottingham Forest until 2030 but will play for Olympiacos this season, including in the Europa League. The transfer negotiations concluded on August 31, 2026, just before the transfer window closed.", "meta": "Gustavo Puerta transfer to Olympiacos Piraeus", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "UEFA announced Olympiacos's full Europa League League Phase schedule for the 2026-27 season. Olympiacos will start at home against Jagiellonia on September 16, 2026, and will host Milan on November 26, 2026. The schedule includes four home and four away matches, with notable away trips to Marseille and Rennes. The team will face Sparta Prague and Hoffenheim at home and conclude the phase away against Torense on January 28, 2027.", "meta": "Olympiacos Piraeus Europa League League Phase schedule", "scope": "Home", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "A verbal agreement has been reached for Gustavo Puerta to become a new player in Vangelis Marinakis's group, with the payment of his release clause. The Colombian will sign for Nottingham Forest and will play this season at Olympiacos to compete in the Europa League.", "meta": "Pip\u00e9 Sierra, Colombian journalist specializing in transfers", "scope": "Home", "context": "Report on the transfer agreement of Gustavo Puerta to Olympiacos Piraeus"}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Volos changed their formation and adopted a more attacking approach in the second half, which allowed them to equalize and seek a winning goal.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Volos' attacking shift in the upcoming match", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "In the first half, Volos focused on defensive solidity by controlling the flanks and preventing Olympiacos from entering their penalty area, but struggled to create meaningful chances in attack.", "meta": "Tactical insight on Volos' first-half defensive strategy in the upcoming match", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Volos hosted Olympiacos Piraeus in a Super League match that ended in a 1-1 draw. The game was marked by a serious injury to Olympiacos's key striker Ayoub El Kaabi, who collided with Volos's goalkeeper Mario Siampanis and had to be stretchered off. Volos managed to secure a valuable point against a strong opponent, continuing their search for a first league win this season. The injury to El Kaabi overshadowed the match and raised concerns for Olympiacos.", "meta": "Volos vs Olympiacos Piraeus match report and injury incident", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Volos prepares to host Olympiacos Piraeus in the third round of the Super League. Volos is still seeking its first league win this season, having drawn recent matches against Iraklis and Kalamata in league and cup competitions. The team has shown fighting spirit but defensive issues remain. Olympiacos aims to continue its winning start to the season. The match offers Volos a chance to challenge a top opponent at home.", "meta": "Volos vs Olympiacos Piraeus Super League match preview", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "insight", "text": "Volos coach Kostas Bratsos commented after the 1-1 draw with Olympiacos that his team dominated both halves of the match but was punished for not scoring more goals. He expressed confusion about the new football rules and highlighted that the team tried to play positively despite the opponent's strength. The draw was a valuable point for Volos as they continue to seek their first league win.", "meta": "Volos coach Kostas Bratsos post-match comments", "scope": "Away", "context": ""}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "From the first half, one team tried to play and the other to destroy. The referee responded accordingly, and I don't know why the new rules exist. We dominated both halves football-wise. Usually in football, you get punished when you don't score goals; we were punished and conceded this goal.", "meta": "Kostas Bratsos, Volos head coach", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match interview after 1-1 draw with Olympiacos Piraeus"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "From the first half, one team tried to play and the other to destroy. In this, the referee responded accordingly, and I don't know why the new rules exist. We dominated both halves football-wise. Usually in football, you get punished when you don't score goals; we were punished and conceded this goal.", "meta": "Kostas Bratsos, Volos head coach", "scope": "Away", "context": "Post-match interview after 1-1 draw with Olympiacos Piraeus"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "I wish a speedy recovery to the two Olympiacos players who are injured. In the first half, we did not allow Olympiacos to enter our penalty area and controlled the flanks. However, we did not create significant chances in the attacking third. The penalty changed the balance. After the break, we changed our structure and decided to play more offensively, which led us to equalize and even look for a comeback.", "meta": "Konstantinos Bratsos, manager of Volos", "scope": "Away", "context": "Volos manager on defensive and offensive adjustments in the upcoming match"}, {"kind": "quote", "text": "Before commenting on the game, I want to express on behalf of the entire Volos organization our deepest condolences to the Mayor of Volos for the loss of his sister. Regarding the match, we managed to come back again. We fell behind undeservedly, punished ourselves by missing chances, and had to make adjustments under pressure. The positive is that we always manage to come back, but we must be more effective and stop disadvantaging ourselves. The effort and unity the players showed on the pitch should not put us in such difficult positions. This game could have been easier if we had finished it by halftime. Also, to those critics on the sidelines, I suggest they look at the x-Goals before commenting.", "meta": "Konstantinos Bratsos, manager of Volos", "scope": "Away", "context": "Volos manager on team resilience and effectiveness before recent Greece Cup game"}]}</script>

